projection verified by page-image collation against the 1962 target edition","provenance_confidence":"high","provenance_evidence":"The project-owned projection passage reproduces the retained calendar body hash exactly. Its artifact manifest records the bounded public-domain 1862 Pustet antecedent, the separate 1962 target, and every editorial transformation; neither witness is represented as owning the projected bytes. The 1962 reading was established on that edition's page images rather than its text layer, cross-read against the Benziger conformed printing. Differences from the antecedent: 1862 sets a colon after `sumpsit`, a semicolon after `effectum` and a colon before `ita nobis`; 1962 sets comma, colon and semicolon respectively; 1862 abbreviates the conclusion to the bare cue `Qui tecum etc.`; 1962 prints `Qui tecum vivit et regnat in unitate.`; j-forms: 1862 `Judas`, `Jesus`; 1862 layer accent damage: `pomam` for `poenam`, `pramiium` for `praemium`, `crrore` for `errore`, `largto-tur` for `largiatur`. Corroboration: the same prayer stands in the 1862 a second time at lines 31274-31289 (Feria V in Coena Domini, printed p. 159) in a cleaner scan, and that second impression supplies every letterform damaged in this one.","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-09-03 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.good-friday-collect","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","normalise consonantal i to the calendar's j orthography","apply the target printing's punctuation","carry the target's conclusion at its printed length"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 162, no. 927; artifact PDF p. 243","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.temporal-good-friday-orations"},"publica